n the current preview is line 983","the preview switches to GOV.UK feedback content at line 984","the current preview therefore exposes 900 data rows from lines 84 through 983 inclusive","Wave113 closes the previously unused contiguous source-line gap 894 through 933","Wave98 covered source lines 834 through 893","Wave105 covered source lines 934 through 983","recent Waves98 113 and105 together now provide continuous QA coverage for source lines 834 through 983","Wave113 contains 40 unique UPRNs and 40 unique source lines","all 40 Wave113 rows are England and East Midlands rows","Wave113 has 16 future_gigabit true rows and 24 future_gigabit false rows while current_gigabit is true on all 40","Wave113 preserves repeated postcodes such as DN36 5JY DN36 5RT and DN41 8ER without treating postcode as premise identity"],"validation_stages":["source","schema","freshness","identity","cardinality","temporal","promotion","fail_closed"]},{"wave":115,"scope":"OS Open UPRN June 2026 current supply and identity audit","source_confidence_percent":99.9,"sources":["https://osdatahub.os.uk/downloads/open/OpenUPRN","https://docs.os.uk/os-downloads/products/addresses-and-names-portfolio/os-open-uprn"],"facts":["OS Open UPRN current version date is June 2026","coverage is all of Great Britain","data structure is vector","supply formats include CSV and GeoPackage","the dataset is free OpenData under the Open Government Licence","the dataset contains UPRNs found in AddressBase Premium","UPRN geometries are supplied in British National Grid","latitude and longitude are also supplied","UPRN is an addressable-location identifier and not broadband availability","OS Open UPRN does not directly expose a Land Registry INSPIRE-ID attribute","UPRN point geometry can support spatial candidate generation","point containment inside an INSPIRE polygon is not legal ownership proof","one polygon can contain more than one UPRN and multiplicity must be preserved","zero UPRNs in a polygon is identity NO_DATA and not broadband NO_SERVICE","no exact parcel broadband promotion occurs from OS Open UPRN coordinates alone"],"validation_stages":["source","schema","freshness","identity","cardinality","temporal","promotion","fail_closed"]},{"wave":116,"scope":"OS Open Linked Identifiers June 2026 relationship audit","source_confidence_percent":99.9,"sources":["https://osdatahub.os.uk/downloads/open/LIDS","https://docs.os.uk/os-downloads/products/buildings-and-infrastructure-portfolio/os-open-linked-identifiers"],"facts":["OS Open Linked Identifiers current version date is June 2026","coverage is all of Great Britain","supply format is CSV","the dataset is freely downloadable OpenData under OGL","it provides authoritative relationships among UPRNs USRNs TOIDs and metadata","the BLPU UPRN TopographicArea TOID 5 GB download is available","the current Data Hub listing shows that GB relationship download at about 842.2 MB","relationship data supports identifier matching but is not broadband availability truth","TOID is a topographic feature identifier and not a Land Registry title number","topographic areas can relate to multiple addressable UPRNs","UPRN TOID relationships do not directly expose HMLR INSPIRE-ID","linked-identifier relationships are separate from legal ownership evidence","version or change confidence must be retained in any later deterministic join","the free relationship route avoids paid HMLR National Polygon access","no UPRN TOID match is promoted to exact parcel broadband without a verified final bridge"],"validation_stages":["source","schema","freshness","identity","cardinality","temporal","promotion","fail_closed"]},{"wave":117,"scope":"HMLR INSPIRE 5 July 2026 current free spatial identity audit","source_confidence_percent":99.9,"sources":["https://use-land-property-data.service.gov.uk/datasets/inspire","https://use-land-property-data.service.gov.uk/datasets/inspire/download","https://use-land-property-data.service.gov.uk/datasets/inspire/tech-guidance"],"facts":["current INSPIRE files were published 5 July 2026","new files are published on the first Sunday of every month","the dataset shows data from the previous month","downloads are listed separately by local authority","the files are published as GML","use and reuse are available under the Open Government Licence","INSPIRE is a subset containing locations of registered freehold property in England and Wales","a polygon on a local-authority boundary can appear in both local-authority files","each polygon has a unique Land Registry INSPIRE ID related to a registered title","one registered title can contain several separate polygons with separate INSPIRE IDs","leasehold and other tenures can be absent from free INSPIRE","INSPIRE polygons show indicative extent and not the definitive legal title boundary","HMLR geometry is captured against British National Grid","HMLR warns reprojection to other coordinate systems can shift some features by up to 15 metres","no authoritative direct public INSPIRE-ID to UPRN crosswalk is exposed by the free dataset"],"validation_stages":["source","schema","freshness","identity","cardinality","temporal","promotion","fail_closed"]},{"wave":118,"scope":"Ofcom Spring 2026 existing coverage and cached archive validation audit","source_confidence_percent":100.0,"sources":["https://www.ofcom.org.uk/phones-and-broadband/coverage-and-speeds/connected-nations-update-spring-2026","https://www.ofcom.org.uk/siteassets/resources/documents/research-and-data/multi-sector/infrastructure-research/connected-nations-spring-2026/about-this-data---fixed-broadband-coverage-and-full-fibre-take-up-2026.pdf?v=417688","github:internet_access_1_ofcom_2026_schema_audit.py","github:internet_access_1_ofcom_2026_schema_audit_runner.py"],"facts":["Ofcom Spring 2026 was published 13 May 2026","the fixed broadband report is a January 2026 snapshot","52 fixed network providers submitted data","18 fixed wireless access providers submitted data","provider submissions cover